-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- LAYER 1, ea3: PART 15, CLAIMS, COMPLAINTS AND INVESTIGATIONS INTO
-- OFFENCES (ss 115 to 126; lines 4612-5010 of EmA1968.txt).
--
-- Source text: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online
-- (inputs/EmA1968.txt).  It is not the official text.  Every `-- src:` line copies a line of that file.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING means the
-- Act does not answer on these facts (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ea3)").  Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- INPUTS.  An input named `the answer of s N` is the answer of another provision of this Part, passed in
-- (PLAN.md section 4).  A list of public holidays is an input wherever the Interpretation Act's s 50(b)
-- moves the last day of a period.  A period that a regulation prescribes is an input.  The Act
-- sets no figure for either, and the encoding takes no figure from outside the Act.

§ `Part 15 -- Claims, complaints and investigations into offences`

§§ `s 115 Commissioner's power to inquire into complaints`

-- s 115(1A): the Commissioner must not inquire into or decide a dispute mentioned in s 115(1) unless the
-- dispute is of a prescribed type, or a claim was lodged in relation to it before 1 April 2017.
-- src:4629 | (1A) The Commissioner must not inquire into or decide a dispute
-- src:4630 | mentioned in subsection (1) unless —
-- src:4632 | (a) the dispute is of a type prescribed by regulations made
-- src:4633 | under section 139; or
-- src:4635 | (b) a claim is lodged under section 119, in relation to the
-- src:4636 | dispute, before 1 April 2017.
@ref s 115(1A) (src:4629-4636)
GIVEN `the dispute is of a type prescribed by regulations made under section 139` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which a claim was lodged under section 119 in relation to the dispute, if one has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(1A) the Commissioner is not barred from inquiring into or deciding the dispute` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the dispute is of a type prescribed by regulations made under section 139` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF lodgedBefore THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commissioner must not inquire into or decide a dispute mentioned in subsection (1) unless —"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        lodgedBefore MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which a claim was lodged under section 119 in relation to the dispute, if one has been`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST lodged THEN lodged LESS THAN Date 1 4 2017

-- s 115(2): "one year" and "6 months" are counted on the calendar.  The corresponding day is the same day of the
-- month; where the month has no such day, the last day of the month (fork F3: the other reading rolls into
-- the next month, as `Date` does).
-- src:4640 | (2) The Commissioner must not inquire into any dispute in respect
-- src:4641 | of matters arising earlier than one year from the date of lodging a
-- src:4642 | claim under section 119 or the termination of the contract of service
-- src:4643 | of or by the person claiming under that section:
@ref s 115(2) (src:4640-4643)
GIVEN event IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 115(2) the corresponding day one year before` MEANS
    `add years` event (0 MINUS 1)

-- src:4645 | Provided that the person claiming in respect of matters arising
-- src:4646 | out of or as the result of a termination of a contract of service has
-- src:4647 | lodged a claim under section 119 within 6 months of the termination
-- src:4648 | of the contract of service.
@ref s 115(2) proviso (src:4645-4648)
GIVEN event IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 115(2) the corresponding day six months after` MEANS
    `add months` event 6

-- The one-year rule counted from one event.
-- src:4640 | (2) The Commissioner must not inquire into any dispute in respect
-- src:4641 | of matters arising earlier than one year from the date of lodging a
-- src:4642 | claim under section 119 or the termination of the contract of service
-- src:4643 | of or by the person claiming under that section:
@ref s 115(2) (src:4640-4643)
GIVEN `the day the matter arose` IS A DATE
      event IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(2) the one-year rule does not bar the matter counted from the event` MEANS
    IF `the day the matter arose` LESS THAN (`s 115(2) the corresponding day one year before` event)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commissioner must not inquire into any dispute in respect of matters arising earlier than one year"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- The proviso: a claim lodged within 6 months of the termination.  Section 50(b) of the Interpretation Act moves the
-- last day if it is a Sunday or a public holiday (fork F4 of the Interpretation Act module; the reading that it
-- reaches every period).
-- src:4645 | Provided that the person claiming in respect of matters arising
-- src:4646 | out of or as the result of a termination of a contract of service has
-- src:4647 | lodged a claim under section 119 within 6 months of the termination
-- src:4648 | of the contract of service.
@ref s 115(2) proviso (src:4645-4648)
GIVEN `the day the contract of service terminated` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 115(2) the last day for lodging a claim within 6 months of the termination` MEANS
    `the last day of the period once section 50(b) is applied` (`s 115(2) the corresponding day six months after` `the day the contract of service terminated`) Months `the public holidays` FALSE

-- src:4640 | (2) The Commissioner must not inquire into any dispute in respect
-- src:4641 | of matters arising earlier than one year from the date of lodging a
-- src:4642 | claim under section 119 or the termination of the contract of service
-- src:4643 | of or by the person claiming under that section:
-- src:4645 | Provided that the person claiming in respect of matters arising
-- src:4646 | out of or as the result of a termination of a contract of service has
-- src:4647 | lodged a claim under section 119 within 6 months of the termination
-- src:4648 | of the contract of service.
@ref s 115(2) (src:4640-4648)
GIVEN `the day the matter arose` IS A DATE
      `the day the claim was lodged under section 119` IS A DATE
      `the day the contract of service terminated, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the matter arose out of or as the result of the termination of the contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(2) the Commissioner is not barred from inquiring into the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER proviso
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST satisfied THEN
        IF satisfied
        THEN yearRule
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Provided that the person claiming in respect of matters arising out of or as the result of a termination of a contract of service has lodged a claim under section 119 within 6 months of the termination" (marginal reading (a): the proviso is a further condition, fork F2)
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        proviso MEANS
            IF `the matter arose out of or as the result of the termination of the contract of service`
            THEN
                CONSIDER `the day the contract of service terminated, if it has`
                -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a matter said to arise out of a termination, with no day of termination given
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                WHEN JUST terminated THEN
                    CONSIDER `s 115(2) the last day for lodging a claim within 6 months of the termination` terminated `the public holidays`
                    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN JUST (`the day the claim was lodged under section 119` AT MOST lastDay)
            ELSE JUST TRUE
        -- "the date of lodging a claim under section 119 or the termination of the contract of service": the text does not say which
        -- of the two events the year is counted from (fork F1), so the answer is given when both readings agree.
        yearRule MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day the contract of service terminated, if it has`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 115(2) the one-year rule does not bar the matter counted from the event` `the day the matter arose` `the day the claim was lodged under section 119`
            WHEN JUST terminated THEN
                IF (`s 115(2) the one-year rule does not bar the matter counted from the event` `the day the matter arose` `the day the claim was lodged under section 119`) EQUALS (`s 115(2) the one-year rule does not bar the matter counted from the event` `the day the matter arose` terminated)
                THEN `s 115(2) the one-year rule does not bar the matter counted from the event` `the day the matter arose` terminated
                -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "the date of lodging a claim under section 119 or the termination of the contract of service" does not say which event the year is counted from, and the two give different answers
                ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4619 | 115.—(1) Subject to this section, the Commissioner may inquire
-- src:4620 | into and decide any dispute between an employee and his or her
-- src:4621 | employer or any person liable under the provisions of this Act to pay
-- src:4622 | any salary due to the employee where the dispute arises out of any
-- src:4623 | term in the contract of service between the employee and his or her
-- src:4624 | employer or out of any of the provisions of this Act, and pursuant to
-- src:4625 | that decision may make an order in the prescribed form for the
-- src:4626 | payment by either party of such sum of money as the Commissioner
-- src:4627 | considers just without limitation of the amount thereof.
@ref s 115(1) (src:4619-4627)
GIVEN `the dispute is between an employee and the employee's employer, or a person liable under the provisions of this Act to pay salary due to the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dispute arises out of a term in the contract of service or out of a provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 115(1A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 115(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(1), (1A) and (2) the Commissioner may inquire into and decide the dispute` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the dispute arises out of any term in the contract of service between the employee and his or her employer or out of any of the provisions of this Act" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05): a dispute arising out of neither is outside the power, whoever the parties are
        IF NOT `the dispute arises out of a term in the contract of service or out of a provision of this Act` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given for a dispute between an employee and the employer or a person liable to pay salary due to the employee; for a dispute between other persons the Act gives no power and does not say there is none (ruling (c), 2026-11-05)
        IF NOT `the dispute is between an employee and the employee's employer, or a person liable under the provisions of this Act to pay salary due to the employee` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commissioner must not inquire into or decide a dispute mentioned in subsection (1) unless" (s 115(1A)); "The Commissioner must not inquire into any dispute in respect of matters arising earlier than one year" (s 115(2))
        IF `the answer of s 115(1A)` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `the answer of s 115(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the bar of subsection (1A) or (2) is itself not answered
        IF `the answer of s 115(1A)` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the answer of s 115(2)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:4619 | 115.—(1) Subject to this section, the Commissioner may inquire
-- src:4620 | into and decide any dispute between an employee and his or her
-- src:4621 | employer or any person liable under the provisions of this Act to pay
-- src:4622 | any salary due to the employee where the dispute arises out of any
-- src:4623 | term in the contract of service between the employee and his or her
-- src:4624 | employer or out of any of the provisions of this Act, and pursuant to
-- src:4625 | that decision may make an order in the prescribed form for the
-- src:4626 | payment by either party of such sum of money as the Commissioner
-- src:4627 | considers just without limitation of the amount thereof.
@ref s 115(1) (src:4619-4627)
GIVEN `the answer of s 115(1), (1A) and (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the order is made pursuant to the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(1) the Commissioner may order payment by the party of such sum as the Commissioner considers just` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the power to order payment is part of the power of s 115(1), (1A) and (2); where that power is not given, neither is this one
        IF `the answer of s 115(1), (1A) and (2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the answer of s 115(1), (1A) and (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the order is made pursuant to the decision` AND `the order is in the prescribed form` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power to order payment is given "pursuant to that decision" and "in the prescribed form"; the Act does not say what the Commissioner may do otherwise
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4650 | (2A) The Commissioner may direct the parties to a dispute
-- src:4651 | mentioned in subsection (1) to attend a mediation conducted by an
-- src:4652 | approved mediator (as defined in section 2(1) of the Employment
-- src:4653 | Claims Act 2016) or a conciliation officer (as defined in section 2 of
-- src:4654 | the Industrial Relations Act 1960).
@ref s 115(2A) (src:4650-4654)
GIVEN `the dispute is one mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mediation is conducted by an approved mediator, as defined in section 2(1) of the Employment Claims Act 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conciliation is conducted by a conciliation officer, as defined in section 2 of the Industrial Relations Act 1960` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(2A) the Commissioner may direct the parties to attend the mediation or conciliation` MEANS
    IF `the dispute is one mentioned in subsection (1)` AND (`the mediation is conducted by an approved mediator, as defined in section 2(1) of the Employment Claims Act 2016` OR `the conciliation is conducted by a conciliation officer, as defined in section 2 of the Industrial Relations Act 1960`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): who is an approved mediator or a conciliation officer is for the Employment Claims Act 2016 and the Industrial Relations Act 1960, which this encoding does not read; the Act says nothing of any other mediator
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4661 | (3) The powers of the Commissioner under subsection (1) include
-- src:4662 | the power to hear and decide, in accordance with the procedure laid
-- src:4663 | down in this Part, any claim by a subcontractor for labour (called in
-- src:4664 | this subsection the claimant) against a contractor or subcontractor for
-- src:4665 | any sum which the claimant claims to be due to the claimant in
-- src:4666 | respect of any labour provided by the claimant under the claimant’s
-- src:4667 | contract with the contractor or subcontractor and to make such
-- src:4668 | consequential orders as may be necessary to give effect to the
-- src:4669 | Commissioner’s decision.
@ref s 115(3) (src:4661-4669)
GIVEN `the claimant is a subcontractor for labour` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is against a contractor or subcontractor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is for a sum claimed to be due in respect of labour provided under the claimant's contract with the contractor or subcontractor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(3) the Commissioner may hear and decide the claim of the subcontractor for labour` MEANS
    IF `the claimant is a subcontractor for labour` AND `the claim is against a contractor or subcontractor` AND `the claim is for a sum claimed to be due in respect of labour provided under the claimant's contract with the contractor or subcontractor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given for the claim of a subcontractor for labour against a contractor or subcontractor for a sum due for labour; the Act does not say what the Commissioner may do about another claim by the same person
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 115(3A): an order for the payment of money in respect of an employee in a managerial or executive position
-- must not exceed $20,000.  For every other employee s 115(1) allows the order "without limitation of the amount".
-- src:4671 | (3A) Where the employee is employed in a managerial or an
-- src:4672 | executive position, an order for the payment of money under
-- src:4673 | subsection (1) must not exceed $20,000.
@ref s 115(3A) (src:4671-4673)
GIVEN `the employee is employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum of money the order is for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(3A) the order for the payment of money is within the limit` MEANS
    IF `the employee is employed in a managerial or an executive position` AND (`the sum of money the order is for` GREATER THAN 20000)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an order for the payment of money under subsection (1) must not exceed $20,000"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- s 115(1): "without limitation of the amount thereof"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4671 | (3A) Where the employee is employed in a managerial or an
-- src:4672 | executive position, an order for the payment of money under
-- src:4673 | subsection (1) must not exceed $20,000.
@ref s 115(3A) (src:4671-4673)
GIVEN `the employee is employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 115(3A) the greatest sum the order for payment may be for` MEANS
    IF `the employee is employed in a managerial or an executive position`
    THEN JUST 20000
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (3A) sets a ceiling only for an employee in a managerial or an executive position; for every other employee s 115(1) says "without limitation of the amount", so NOTHING here means no ceiling is stated
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4685 | (3C) An application to set aside or vary an order made by the
-- src:4686 | Commissioner referred to in subsection (3B) must be made no later
-- src:4687 | than 14 days after the date of the order.
@ref s 115(3C) (src:4685-4687)
GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE
      `the day the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(3C) the application is made no later than 14 days after the date of the order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the period once section 50(b) is applied` (`the day of the order` PLUS 14) Days `the public holidays` FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
        IF `the day the application is made` AT MOST lastDay
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application to set aside or vary an order ... must be made no later than 14 days after the date of the order"
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The last day on which the application may be made: 14 days after the date of the order, moved by the Interpretation
-- Act's s 50(b) when it falls on an excluded day.
-- src:4685 | (3C) An application to set aside or vary an order made by the
-- src:4686 | Commissioner referred to in subsection (3B) must be made no later
-- src:4687 | than 14 days after the date of the order.
@ref s 115(3C) (src:4685-4687)
GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 115(3C) the last day for making the application` MEANS
    `the last day of the period once section 50(b) is applied` (`the day of the order` PLUS 14) Days `the public holidays` FALSE

-- src:4677 | (3B) Subject to subsection (3C), any order made by the
-- src:4678 | Commissioner under subsection (1) in the absence of a party
-- src:4679 | concerned or affected by the order may be set aside or varied by
-- src:4680 | the Commissioner, on the application of that party, on such terms as
-- src:4681 | the Commissioner thinks just.
-- src:4685 | (3C) An application to set aside or vary an order made by the
-- src:4686 | Commissioner referred to in subsection (3B) must be made no later
-- src:4687 | than 14 days after the date of the order.
@ref s 115(3B) and (3C) (src:4677-4687)
GIVEN `the order was made under subsection (1) in the absence of a party concerned or affected by the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by that party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 115(3C)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(3B) and (3C) the Commissioner may set aside or vary the order on the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3B) gives the power for an order made in the absence of a party, on that party's application
        IF NOT (`the order was made under subsection (1) in the absence of a party concerned or affected by the order` AND `the application is made by that party`) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (3C)" and "must be made no later than 14 days after the date of the order"
        IF `the answer of s 115(3C)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the time limit of subsection (3C) is itself not answered
        IF `the answer of s 115(3C)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 115(4): "employer" includes the transferor and the transferee of an undertaking (or part of one) referred to in s 18A.
-- src:4691 | (4) In this section, “employer” includes the transferor and the
-- src:4692 | transferee of an undertaking or part thereof referred to in section 18A.
@ref s 115(4) (src:4691-4692)
GIVEN `the person is the transferor or the transferee of an undertaking or part of an undertaking referred to in section 18A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 2(1) "employer"` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(4) "employer" the person is one` MEANS
    IF `the person is the transferor or the transferee of an undertaking or part of an undertaking referred to in section 18A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes the transferor and the transferee" opens the class, so a person who is neither is left to the answer of s 2(1)
    ELSE `the answer of s 2(1) "employer"`

§§ `s 116 Prohibiting order by Commissioner to third party`

-- src:4696 | 116.—(1) Whenever the Commissioner has made an order under
-- src:4697 | section 115 against any employer or any person liable for the payment
-- src:4698 | of any sum of money to any workman or subcontractor for labour and
-- src:4699 | after inquiry finds that there exists between that employer or person
-- src:4700 | liable and some other person a contract in the course of the execution
-- src:4701 | of which the workman or subcontractor for labour performed the
-- src:4702 | work in respect of which the order has been made, the Commissioner
-- src:4703 | may summon that other person and may make an order prohibiting
-- src:4704 | that other person from paying to the employer or person liable and
-- src:4705 | requiring that other person to pay to the Commissioner any money
-- src:4710 | (not exceeding the amount found due to the workman or
-- src:4711 | subcontractor for labour) admitted by that other person to be owing
-- src:4712 | to the employer or person liable in respect of the contract.
@ref s 116(1) (src:4696-4712)
GIVEN `the Commissioner has made an order under section 115 against an employer, or a person liable for the payment of a sum of money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum of money is payable to a workman or subcontractor for labour` IS A BOOLEAN
      `after inquiry the Commissioner finds that a contract exists between the employer or person liable and another person, in the course of whose execution the workman or subcontractor for labour did the work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116(1) the Commissioner may order the other person to pay the money to the Commissioner` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner has made an order under section 115 against an employer, or a person liable for the payment of a sum of money` AND `the sum of money is payable to a workman or subcontractor for labour` AND `after inquiry the Commissioner finds that a contract exists between the employer or person liable and another person, in the course of whose execution the workman or subcontractor for labour did the work`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Whenever the Commissioner has made an order under section 115 against any employer or any person liable for the payment of any sum of money to any workman or subcontractor for labour and after inquiry finds that there exists ... a contract" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05: "whenever" counts as "where"); an order for a sum payable to an employee who is not a workman is outside it, which is assumed to be the text's own "no" and not a scope limit (fork F28)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The money the other person is to pay: what that person admits to be owing to the employer or person liable,
-- not more than the amount found due to the workman or subcontractor for labour.
-- src:4696 | 116.—(1) Whenever the Commissioner has made an order under
-- src:4697 | section 115 against any employer or any person liable for the payment
-- src:4698 | of any sum of money to any workman or subcontractor for labour and
-- src:4699 | after inquiry finds that there exists between that employer or person
-- src:4700 | liable and some other person a contract in the course of the execution
-- src:4701 | of which the workman or subcontractor for labour performed the
-- src:4702 | work in respect of which the order has been made, the Commissioner
-- src:4703 | may summon that other person and may make an order prohibiting
-- src:4704 | that other person from paying to the employer or person liable and
-- src:4705 | requiring that other person to pay to the Commissioner any money
-- src:4710 | (not exceeding the amount found due to the workman or
-- src:4711 | subcontractor for labour) admitted by that other person to be owing
-- src:4712 | to the employer or person liable in respect of the contract.
@ref s 116(1) (src:4696-4712)
GIVEN `the amount found due to the workman or subcontractor for labour` IS A NUMBER
      `the money admitted by the other person to be owing to the employer or person liable in respect of the contract` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 116(1) the greatest sum the order may require the other person to pay to the Commissioner` MEANS
    min `the amount found due to the workman or subcontractor for labour` `the money admitted by the other person to be owing to the employer or person liable in respect of the contract`

-- src:4714 | (2) Where that other person admits to the Commissioner in writing
-- src:4715 | that money is owing by that other person under the contract to the
-- src:4716 | employer or person liable, that other person need not be summoned
-- src:4717 | before the Commissioner and the Commissioner may make such
-- src:4718 | order in that other person’s absence.
@ref s 116(2) (src:4714-4718)
GIVEN `the other person admits to the Commissioner in writing that money is owing under the contract to the employer or person liable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116(2) the other person need not be summoned before the Commissioner` MEANS
    IF `the other person admits to the Commissioner in writing that money is owing under the contract to the employer or person liable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where that other person admits to the Commissioner in writing that money is owing" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05): without a written admission the relief of subsection (2) does not apply, and subsection (1) ("the Commissioner may summon") governs; JUST FALSE here is not "must be summoned"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 116(3): where the other person is liable as a principal under s 65 and the money admitted is not enough to pay the
-- whole salary, nothing in the subsection relieves that person of liability for the balance.
-- src:4720 | (3) Where that other person is liable as a principal under section 65
-- src:4721 | to pay any salary due by the employer or person liable and where the
-- src:4722 | money admitted by that other person to be owing to the employer or
-- src:4723 | person liable is not sufficient to pay the whole of the salary, nothing in
-- src:4724 | this subsection relieves that other person of that other person’s
-- src:4725 | liability for the balance of the salary up to the amount for which that
-- src:4726 | other person is liable under that section.
@ref s 116(3) (src:4720-4726)
GIVEN `the answer of s 65 the principal is liable to pay the salary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the salary due by the employer or person liable` IS A NUMBER
      `the money admitted by the other person to be owing to the employer or person liable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116(3) the other person is relieved of liability for the balance of the salary` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of the other person who is liable as a principal under section 65 where the money admitted is not sufficient; it says nothing of any other case
        IF `the answer of s 65 the principal is liable to pay the salary` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (`the answer of s 65 the principal is liable to pay the salary` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (`the money admitted by the other person to be owing to the employer or person liable` LESS THAN `the salary due by the employer or person liable`)) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this subsection relieves that other person of that other person's liability for the balance of the salary"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:4720 | (3) Where that other person is liable as a principal under section 65
-- src:4721 | to pay any salary due by the employer or person liable and where the
-- src:4722 | money admitted by that other person to be owing to the employer or
-- src:4723 | person liable is not sufficient to pay the whole of the salary, nothing in
-- src:4724 | this subsection relieves that other person of that other person’s
-- src:4725 | liability for the balance of the salary up to the amount for which that
-- src:4726 | other person is liable under that section.
@ref s 116(3) (src:4720-4726)
GIVEN `the answer of s 65 the principal is liable to pay the salary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the amount for which the other person is liable under section 65` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the salary due by the employer or person liable` IS A NUMBER
      `the money admitted by the other person to be owing to the employer or person liable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 116(3) the balance of the salary for which the other person remains liable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the answer of s 65 the principal is liable to pay the salary` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (`the money admitted by the other person to be owing to the employer or person liable` LESS THAN `the salary due by the employer or person liable`)) THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the amount for which the other person is liable under section 65`
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "up to the amount for which that other person is liable under that section" is the answer of section 65
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST ceiling THEN JUST (min (`the salary due by the employer or person liable` MINUS `the money admitted by the other person to be owing to the employer or person liable`) ceiling)

-- src:4728 | (4) Any person so summoned is legally bound to attend at the time
-- src:4729 | and place mentioned in the summons and to answer truthfully all
-- src:4730 | questions relating to the contract which the Commissioner may put to
-- src:4731 | that person.
@ref s 116(4) (src:4728-4731)
GIVEN `the person has been summoned by the Commissioner under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116(4) the person summoned is legally bound to attend at the time and place mentioned in the summons` MEANS
    IF `the person has been summoned by the Commissioner under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "any person so summoned"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4728 | (4) Any person so summoned is legally bound to attend at the time
-- src:4729 | and place mentioned in the summons and to answer truthfully all
-- src:4730 | questions relating to the contract which the Commissioner may put to
-- src:4731 | that person.
@ref s 116(4) (src:4728-4731)
GIVEN `the person has been summoned by the Commissioner under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question relates to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116(4) the person summoned is legally bound to answer the question truthfully` MEANS
    IF `the person has been summoned by the Commissioner under this section` AND `the question relates to the contract`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is to answer "all questions relating to the contract"; the Act does not say the person need not answer another question
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4733 | (5) The payment of any money pursuant to an order under
-- src:4734 | subsection (1) is a discharge and payment up to the amount so paid
-- src:4735 | of money due to the employer or person liable under the contract.
@ref s 116(5) (src:4733-4735)
GIVEN `the money paid pursuant to an order under subsection (1)` IS A NUMBER
      `the money due to the employer or person liable under the contract` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 116(5) the amount of the money due under the contract that the payment discharges` MEANS
    min `the money paid pursuant to an order under subsection (1)` `the money due to the employer or person liable under the contract`

§§ `s 117 Right of appeal`

-- s 117(1): within 14 days after the decision or order; the Interpretation Act's s 50(b) moves a last day that
-- falls on an excluded day.
-- src:4739 | 117.—(1) Where any person interested is dissatisfied with the
-- src:4740 | decision or order of the Commissioner, the person may, within
-- src:4741 | 14 days after the decision or order, appeal to the General Division of
-- src:4742 | the High Court from the decision or order.
@ref s 117(1) (src:4739-4742)
GIVEN `the day of the decision or order` IS A DATE
      `the day the appeal is made` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117(1) the appeal is made within 14 days after the decision or order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the period once section 50(b) is applied` (`the day of the decision or order` PLUS 14) Days `the public holidays` FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
        IF `the day the appeal is made` AT MOST lastDay
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the person may, within 14 days after the decision or order, appeal" (ruling (a), 2026-11-05, which overrules fork F7): an appeal made after the last day is outside the period
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4739 | 117.—(1) Where any person interested is dissatisfied with the
-- src:4740 | decision or order of the Commissioner, the person may, within
-- src:4741 | 14 days after the decision or order, appeal to the General Division of
-- src:4742 | the High Court from the decision or order.
@ref s 117(1) (src:4739-4742)
GIVEN `the person is interested and dissatisfied with the decision or order of the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 117(1) within 14 days` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117(1) the person may appeal to the General Division of the High Court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any person interested is dissatisfied with the decision or order of the Commissioner, the person may ... appeal" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05): a person who is not interested and dissatisfied is outside it
        IF NOT `the person is interested and dissatisfied with the decision or order of the Commissioner` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE `the answer of s 117(1) within 14 days`

-- The court to which the appeal lies is named in the same subsection.
-- src:4739 | 117.—(1) Where any person interested is dissatisfied with the
-- src:4740 | decision or order of the Commissioner, the person may, within
-- src:4741 | 14 days after the decision or order, appeal to the General Division of
-- src:4742 | the High Court from the decision or order.
@ref s 117(1) (src:4739-4742)
GIVEN `the answer of s 117(1) the person may appeal` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Official or body the Act names`
`s 117(1) the court to which the appeal lies` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 117(1) the person may appeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST `Body: the General Division of the High Court`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names the court only for the appeal it gives; where it gives none it names no court
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4746 | (2) The procedure governing any such appeal to the General
-- src:4747 | Division of the High Court is as provided for in the Rules of Court.
@ref s 117(2) (src:4746-4747)
GIVEN `the proceeding is an appeal to the General Division of the High Court from a decision or order of the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117(2) the procedure governing the appeal is as provided for in the Rules of Court` MEANS
    IF `the proceeding is an appeal to the General Division of the High Court from a decision or order of the Commissioner`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the procedure itself is in the Rules of Court, which are not in the text; TRUE here says only that the Rules of Court govern
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 118 Fees and enforcement of orders`

DECLARE `s 118(1) Kind of fee` IS ONE OF
    `s 118(1) the registration fee at the rate in the Second Schedule`
    `s 118(1) a fee of any other kind`

-- src:4753 | 118.—(1) No fees other than a registration fee in accordance with
-- src:4754 | the rates specified in the Second Schedule are to be charged by the
-- src:4759 | Commissioner in respect of processes issued by the Commissioner
-- src:4760 | under this Part and all orders made by the Commissioner, even though
@ref s 118(1) (src:4753-4760)
GIVEN fee IS A `s 118(1) Kind of fee`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 118(1) the Commissioner may charge the fee` MEANS
    CONSIDER fee
    WHEN `s 118(1) the registration fee at the rate in the Second Schedule` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No fees other than a registration fee in accordance with the rates specified in the Second Schedule are to be charged by the Commissioner"
    WHEN `s 118(1) a fee of any other kind` THEN JUST FALSE

-- src:4759 | Commissioner in respect of processes issued by the Commissioner
-- src:4760 | under this Part and all orders made by the Commissioner, even though
-- src:4761 | they may in respect of the amount or value be in excess of the
-- src:4762 | ordinary jurisdiction of the court, are to be enforced by a District
-- src:4763 | Court in the same manner as a judgment of that Court and all
-- src:4764 | necessary processes may be served by the Court on the
-- src:4765 | Commissioner’s behalf.
@ref s 118(1) (src:4759-4765)
GIVEN `the order was made by the Commissioner under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 118(1) the order made by the Commissioner is enforced by a District Court` MEANS
    IF `the order was made by the Commissioner under this Part`
    -- "even though they may in respect of the amount or value be in excess of the ordinary jurisdiction of the court"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the enforcement is of "all orders made by the Commissioner" under this Part
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4767 | (2) A sale of immovable property must not be ordered for the
-- src:4768 | purposes of the enforcement, except by the General Division of the
-- src:4769 | High Court.
@ref s 118(2) (src:4767-4769)
GIVEN body IS A `Official or body the Act names`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 118(2) the body may order a sale of immovable property for the purposes of the enforcement` MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `Body: the General Division of the High Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A sale of immovable property must not be ordered for the purposes of the enforcement, except by the General Division of the High Court"
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 119 Procedure for making and hearing claims`

-- src:4778 | (a) the person claiming must lodge a memorandum at the
-- src:4779 | office of the Commissioner, specifying shortly the subject
-- src:4780 | matter of the claim and the remedy sought to be obtained,
-- src:4781 | or the person may make a claim in person to the
-- src:4782 | Commissioner who must immediately reduce it or cause
-- src:4783 | it to be reduced in writing;
@ref s 119(1)(a) (src:4778-4783)
GIVEN `a memorandum specifying shortly the subject matter of the claim and the remedy sought has been lodged at the office of the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim has been made in person to the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 119(1)(a) the claim is made in a way that paragraph (a) provides` MEANS
    IF `a memorandum specifying shortly the subject matter of the claim and the remedy sought has been lodged at the office of the Commissioner` OR `the claim has been made in person to the Commissioner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) names two ways of making a claim and does not say that no other way is good
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4778 | (a) the person claiming must lodge a memorandum at the
