    IF `the Commissioner has received the memorandum or verbal claim` AND `the Commissioner has received the registration fee payable in accordance with the Second Schedule`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "upon receipt of the memorandum or verbal claim and of the registration fee payable" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05: "upon" counts as "where"); with either not received the duty has not arisen, as "upon payment of the prescribed fee" does for paragraph (j)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4785 | (b) upon receipt of the memorandum or verbal claim and of the
