    IF `the person is a witness that either party wishes to call`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to summon "such witnesses as either party may wish to call"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Fork F5: "not less than 3 days before the date of the inquiry" is read as a gap of at least 3 days between the
-- day of the notice and the day of the inquiry; the other reading counts 3 clear days between them.
-- src:4799 | (d) if the party against whom a claim is made wishes to make a
-- src:4800 | counterclaim against the party claiming, the firstmentioned
-- src:4801 | party must notify the Commissioner and the other party in
-- src:4806 | writing of the nature and amount of the counterclaim not
-- src:4807 | less than 3 days before the date of the inquiry;
@ref s 119(1)(d) (src:4799-4807)
GIVEN `the day the notice of the counterclaim is given` IS A DATE
      `the day of the inquiry` IS A DATE
      `the notice is in writing and states the nature and amount of the counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 119(1)(d) the notice of the counterclaim is given not less than 3 days before the date of the inquiry` MEANS
    IF `the notice is in writing and states the nature and amount of the counterclaim` AND (((Day `the day of the inquiry`) MINUS (Day `the day the notice of the counterclaim is given`)) AT LEAST 3)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the firstmentioned party must notify the Commissioner and the other party in writing of the nature and amount of the counterclaim not less than 3 days before the date of the inquiry"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Paragraph (e), the Commissioner's power: "at any time between the issuing of summons and the hearing of the claim" is a
-- period the text fixes in its own words (ruling (a), 2026-11-05).  Both ends are read as inside it (fork F28).
-- src:4809 | (e) at any time between the issuing of summons and the
-- src:4810 | hearing of the claim, the Commissioner may hold or cause
-- src:4811 | to be held a preliminary inquiry at which the party claiming
-- src:4812 | and the party against whom the claim is made must be
-- src:4813 | present after having been notified in writing of the inquiry;
@ref s 119(1)(e) (src:4809-4813)
GIVEN `the day the summons was issued` IS A DATE
      `the day of the hearing of the claim` IS A DATE
      `the day of the preliminary inquiry` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 119(1)(e) the Commissioner may hold a preliminary inquiry on the day` MEANS
    IF (`the day the summons was issued` AT MOST `the day of the preliminary inquiry`) AND (`the day of the preliminary inquiry` AT MOST `the day of the hearing of the claim`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time between the issuing of summons and the hearing of the claim, the Commissioner may hold or cause to be held a preliminary inquiry" (ruling (a), 2026-11-05)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4809 | (e) at any time between the issuing of summons and the
-- src:4810 | hearing of the claim, the Commissioner may hold or cause
-- src:4811 | to be held a preliminary inquiry at which the party claiming
-- src:4812 | and the party against whom the claim is made must be
-- src:4813 | present after having been notified in writing of the inquiry;
@ref s 119(1)(e) (src:4809-4813)
GIVEN `the Commissioner holds a preliminary inquiry between the issuing of summons and the hearing of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has been notified in writing of the inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 119(1)(e) the party must be present at the preliminary inquiry` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner holds a preliminary inquiry between the issuing of summons and the hearing of the claim` AND `the party has been notified in writing of the inquiry`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the parties "must be present after having been notified in writing"; the Act does not say what follows for a party not so notified
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 119(1)(f) Step at the preliminary inquiry` IS ONE OF
    `s 119(1)(f) amend the whole claim or a portion of it`
    `s 119(1)(f) withdraw the whole claim or a portion of it`
    `s 119(1)(f) make a counterclaim`
    `s 119(1)(f) reach a settlement in respect of the claim`
    `s 119(1)(f) a step of some other kind`

